WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.250
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:06.520 --> 00:09.120
Are you sure if we put on an act,

3
00:09.200 --> 00:10.240
the ghost will be stupid enough to believe us?

4
00:10.320 --> 00:12.680
You just have to make it convincing enough for it to believe us.

5
00:15.120 --> 00:17.880
You usually look so dead inside when talking to clients.

6
00:17.960 --> 00:19.440
What's gotten into you, Vann?

7
00:19.520 --> 00:22.880
From now on, if you're sad, look at this bracelet and think of me instead.

8
00:22.960 --> 00:24.240
You don't have to think about anyone else.

9
00:24.320 --> 00:25.240
Rakkhun.

10
00:25.320 --> 00:26.560
We're still together, right?

11
00:27.200 --> 00:28.280
Kan came to talk to me.

12
00:29.000 --> 00:30.000
What do you think I should do?

13
00:31.560 --> 00:32.840
Why are you scared?

14
00:32.920 --> 00:35.480
The ghost… is the one who should be scared of me.

15
00:41.680 --> 00:42.800
You're leaving already?

16
00:42.880 --> 00:44.920
If that's all you're going to do, don't bother coming.

17
00:45.000 --> 00:46.000
What a waste of time.

18
00:46.080 --> 00:48.520
Vann! What are you doing?

19
00:49.640 --> 00:50.520
Aw!

20
00:50.600 --> 00:52.040
I thought you'd be scarier than this.

21
00:52.120 --> 00:53.680
Come out and let me see you if you dare.

22
00:53.760 --> 00:54.800
Don't just make noises.

23
00:54.880 --> 00:57.160
And did you turn off the lights to boost the damage?

24
00:57.240 --> 00:58.920
It's not scary at all.

25
00:59.000 --> 01:00.720
Save that trick for scaring kids.

26
01:00.800 --> 01:01.920
Rakkhun.

27
01:02.000 --> 01:03.960
How about we go public as a couple?

28
01:04.040 --> 01:06.200
And when you graduate, we'll get married.

29
01:15.280 --> 01:18.440
Vann. What's wrong with you?

30
01:21.400 --> 01:23.360
Took you long enough to show yourself.

31
01:24.040 --> 01:25.800
You kept me waiting so long.

32
01:26.480 --> 01:27.640
Get out.

33
01:29.960 --> 01:31.560
Where do you expect me to go?

34
01:32.080 --> 01:34.440
You're choking me.

35
01:35.920 --> 01:37.640
Go die wherever you want.

36
01:37.720 --> 01:39.600
What are you saying?

37
01:39.680 --> 01:41.040
I can't understand you.

38
01:41.960 --> 01:44.360
What's your name? What do you want?

39
01:44.440 --> 01:45.560
Tell me.

40
01:47.680 --> 01:49.600
You have to stay away from Rakkhun.

41
01:50.120 --> 01:52.040
Otherwise, I'll kill you.

42
01:53.960 --> 01:55.160
Vann!

43
01:55.240 --> 01:56.360
What happened?

44
01:57.440 --> 01:58.560
I'm scared.

45
02:00.600 --> 02:06.120
Tell him that Garlah will kill you.

46
02:15.800 --> 02:18.360
Vann. Are you okay?

47
02:18.960 --> 02:20.720
I'm fine. I'm okay.

48
02:21.240 --> 02:22.360
Don't worry about me.

49
02:23.000 --> 02:23.920
Your neck.

50
02:25.040 --> 02:26.320
Your neck.

51
03:30.680 --> 03:32.320
You really won't go to the hospital?

52
03:33.440 --> 03:34.720
I can take you.

53
03:37.000 --> 03:38.120
No.

54
03:38.200 --> 03:39.880
Just take care of me. That's enough.

55
03:40.800 --> 03:42.240
Don't even start.

56
03:42.960 --> 03:45.400
How could you provoke her like that?

57
03:45.480 --> 03:47.840
What if she really snapped your neck?

58
03:47.920 --> 03:49.560
What would you do?

59
03:51.360 --> 03:52.240
Come on.

60
03:52.840 --> 03:54.520
My neck didn't come off.

61
03:56.080 --> 03:58.360
At least now I know her name is Garlah.

62
03:59.280 --> 04:00.240
It was worth it.

63
04:00.320 --> 04:02.960
You risked that much just to learn her name?

64
04:03.680 --> 04:05.200
How does knowing that help you?

65
04:05.920 --> 04:08.440
At least the fact that Garlah showed herself to me

66
04:08.520 --> 04:11.080
means she believes we're together.

67
04:11.160 --> 04:12.960
Now you don't have to worry.

68
04:13.040 --> 04:14.400
I'll talk to her.

69
04:15.000 --> 04:17.079
You'll definitely get to live the life you want.

70
04:20.320 --> 04:21.720
But go to sleep now.

71
04:21.800 --> 04:22.760
I'll keep working on the model.

72
04:23.440 --> 04:24.720
I can't sleep.

73
04:25.840 --> 04:27.320
The knife is still stuck in the model.

74
04:29.800 --> 04:30.720
Seriously, Vann.

75
04:30.800 --> 04:32.360
I don't want to sleep here at all.

76
04:33.320 --> 04:35.400
Didn't you say she could follow you anywhere?

77
04:36.040 --> 04:37.000
That's right.

78
04:37.920 --> 04:39.600
But I can't sleep.

79
04:45.640 --> 04:47.760
If it's somewhere else, you'll be able to sleep, right?

80
04:57.800 --> 04:58.760
Come in.

81
05:03.160 --> 05:04.600
Whoa.

82
05:05.280 --> 05:06.480
Are all these yours?

83
05:07.240 --> 05:08.280
Yeah.

84
05:08.360 --> 05:10.160
I saved up and bought them myself.

85
05:10.760 --> 05:12.080
Some of them have been discontinued.

86
05:14.240 --> 05:15.840
You're such a nerd.

87
05:20.040 --> 05:21.120
Whoa.

88
05:21.640 --> 05:22.640
Hey!

89
05:23.240 --> 05:25.480
You can look, but don't touch. They might break.

90
05:26.080 --> 05:27.640
These things are delicate.

91
05:28.240 --> 05:30.040
Wow. You're really protective of them.

92
05:30.640 --> 05:31.600
Of course I am.

93
05:31.680 --> 05:33.120
Each one was so hard to get.

94
05:34.320 --> 05:36.680
Some of them almost ended up at the dump.

95
05:36.760 --> 05:37.800
Luckily, I got to them in time.

96
05:39.440 --> 05:40.800
Go shower and get some sleep.

97
05:40.880 --> 05:43.320
You sleep on the bed tonight.

98
05:43.400 --> 05:44.840
I'll sleep on the floor.

99
05:44.920 --> 05:46.000
No.

100
05:46.600 --> 05:47.440
You sleep on the bed.

101
05:47.520 --> 05:48.680
I'll sleep on the floor.

102
05:48.760 --> 05:50.000
No way.

103
05:50.520 --> 05:54.720
I have to take good care of my super VVIP client.

104
05:59.040 --> 06:00.440
Go take a shower.

105
06:00.520 --> 06:01.520
Go, go, go!

106
06:02.520 --> 06:03.640
Fine, I'll go.

107
06:23.480 --> 06:24.360
Sorry.

108
06:24.440 --> 06:26.080
I'll lower it for you.

109
06:59.240 --> 07:00.560
Is the light bothering your eyes?

110
07:00.640 --> 07:02.040
Should I move somewhere else to work on it?

111
07:04.560 --> 07:05.640
It's fine.

112
07:09.480 --> 07:11.200
I can't sleep anyway.

113
07:15.280 --> 07:16.520
Want me to help?

114
07:17.960 --> 07:19.840
Didn't you tell me you'd be able to sleep somewhere else?

115
07:21.920 --> 07:24.000
I do feel more at ease here than in my room.

116
07:25.000 --> 07:28.440
But I feel bad if you do it alone.

117
07:30.120 --> 07:32.200
I'm chill. Don't overthink it.

118
07:32.720 --> 07:34.080
This is my job.

119
07:34.600 --> 07:36.080
Once this job is done, I get paid.

120
07:36.160 --> 07:37.480
See? It's a win-win for both of us.

121
07:44.480 --> 07:46.680
Hey, did I say something wrong?

122
07:47.280 --> 07:48.680
No.

123
07:54.960 --> 07:56.120
Can I ask you something?

124
07:57.120 --> 07:58.960
Why did you join the Crow Club?

125
08:01.120 --> 08:03.080
I don't really want to use this word, but…

126
08:05.280 --> 08:06.840
I guess it was fate.

127
08:07.440 --> 08:08.920
My life was terrible back then.

128
08:09.520 --> 08:11.040
I got fired.

129
08:11.840 --> 08:13.320
And I didn't get the scholarship.

130
08:14.680 --> 08:16.320
But I happened to meet Linda.

131
08:18.560 --> 08:20.200
When Linda offered me a job at the club,

132
08:20.960 --> 08:25.280
at first, I wondered what kind of job paid this much.

133
08:25.360 --> 08:27.240
But I had nothing left to lose.

134
08:28.280 --> 08:31.520
As long as I could earn money legally, I'd do any job.

135
08:32.440 --> 08:34.080
And it really does pay a lot.

136
08:35.120 --> 08:36.880
Even if the jobs are a little weird.

137
08:41.840 --> 08:43.559
Oh, you…

138
08:43.640 --> 08:45.600
When you're ready to sleep, you fall asleep so easily.

139
08:53.840 --> 08:55.200
Why am I smiling?

140
08:56.360 --> 08:57.600
Damn it!

141
09:46.960 --> 09:49.000
Your face is so red. Are you okay?

142
09:51.080 --> 09:52.720
And why are you sleeping here?

143
09:54.600 --> 09:56.400
Someone fell asleep last night.

144
09:56.920 --> 09:58.160
And then…

145
09:59.520 --> 10:01.320
you held my hand and wouldn't let go.

146
10:02.560 --> 10:05.400
"Stay here. Don't leave me."

147
10:06.200 --> 10:07.520
You're exaggerating.

148
10:11.280 --> 10:15.000
Didn't you put your hand in mine yourself and then make the whole thing up?

149
10:15.680 --> 10:17.040
There's a camera in my room.

150
10:17.120 --> 10:18.600
Want me to pull up the footage?

151
10:19.600 --> 10:20.720
No need.

152
10:21.880 --> 10:23.120
I'm going to take a shower.

153
10:24.360 --> 10:25.320
I'm not talking to you anymore.

154
10:27.120 --> 10:28.480
Hey, that's the blanket.

155
10:28.560 --> 10:30.440
Where are you taking it?

156
10:34.640 --> 10:35.480
Yeah.

157
10:41.280 --> 10:42.440
Hurry up and shower.

158
10:42.520 --> 10:43.840
I'll take you to get something to eat.

159
10:50.160 --> 10:51.640
Mimi, can I have another chicken thigh?

160
10:52.520 --> 10:54.040
There's only one chicken thigh.

161
10:54.120 --> 10:56.160
You had the chicken thigh the other day too.

162
10:56.240 --> 10:57.080
-Hey, how could you do this? -We're eating.

163
10:57.160 --> 10:58.640
Can I have some too?

164
10:58.720 --> 11:00.040
What's there to eat today?

165
11:00.120 --> 11:01.360
Look. Can't you see?

166
11:01.440 --> 11:02.440
Whoa!

167
11:02.520 --> 11:04.560
Linda made a lot of food today.

168
11:04.640 --> 11:06.080
Is she planning to feed the whole neighborhood?

169
11:06.680 --> 11:07.760
Sit down.

170
11:14.280 --> 11:15.840
What? What are you guys looking at?

171
11:19.720 --> 11:20.760
Hey.

172
11:20.840 --> 11:22.560
If you're going to go public,

173
11:22.640 --> 11:24.360
shouldn't you introduce him first?

174
11:25.080 --> 11:26.040
He gets here and you just let him sit?

175
11:27.440 --> 11:29.160
Hi, nice to meet you.

176
11:29.240 --> 11:31.120
I'm Mimi.

177
11:31.200 --> 11:32.400
Hi, I'm Rakkhun.

178
11:32.480 --> 11:33.760
You can call me Rak.

179
11:34.360 --> 11:35.520
Rakkhun?

180
11:35.600 --> 11:36.720
Your name is so unique.

181
11:37.320 --> 11:40.920
I can't believe someone as foul-mouthed as Vann

182
11:41.000 --> 11:42.880
could actually have a boyfriend.

183
11:43.480 --> 11:45.200
Not a boyfriend. He's a client, damn it.

184
11:49.040 --> 11:50.440
Is he really our client?

185
11:51.640 --> 11:52.720
He's our client?

186
11:58.200 --> 11:59.440
-Come here. -What?

187
12:00.080 --> 12:01.800
You brought a client to sleep at the club?

188
12:03.520 --> 12:05.440
Why did Linda never tell us we could do that?

189
12:05.520 --> 12:06.920
I would've done it too.

190
12:07.520 --> 12:09.720
Vann. Are you crazy?

191
12:09.800 --> 12:11.360
Did you forget Linda's golden rule?

192
12:12.240 --> 12:13.400
Yeah, Vann.

193
12:13.480 --> 12:15.840
If any Crow crosses the line

194
12:15.920 --> 12:18.440
and gets so involved with a client that they can't separate the two,

195
12:18.520 --> 12:20.200
they'll be kicked out.

196
12:20.960 --> 12:21.960
You guys are getting carried away.

197
12:22.040 --> 12:24.520
I brought him here because of work.

198
12:24.600 --> 12:27.200
And I already got Linda's permission.

199
12:28.320 --> 12:29.440
And she gave you permission?

200
12:30.560 --> 12:32.480
She's playing favorites.

201
12:32.560 --> 12:35.120
I'm sorry, everyone, for disturbing you.

202
12:35.720 --> 12:37.280
I might be staying here for a while.

203
12:37.800 --> 12:39.240
Until Vann finishes this job.

204
12:41.040 --> 12:43.800
You don't have to apologize, Rakkhun.

205
12:43.880 --> 12:47.000
Having another handsome guy join our club,

206
12:47.080 --> 12:50.240
I'm more than happy about it.

207
12:50.320 --> 12:51.480
Are you tired? Did you travel far?

208
12:51.560 --> 12:54.080
-I'm not tired. -If you're tired, eat plenty.

209
12:54.160 --> 12:56.080
Go on, eat. Here, I'll feed you.

210
12:57.920 --> 12:59.280
Make yourself at home, Rakkhun.

211
12:59.800 --> 13:01.200
The Crow Club welcomes you.

212
13:01.280 --> 13:02.400
Thank you.

213
13:03.720 --> 13:05.720
Since you've moved in here,

214
13:07.080 --> 13:08.680
does that mean you've seen the ghost?

215
13:08.760 --> 13:10.000
I have.

216
13:10.080 --> 13:11.600
Her name is Garlah.

217
13:12.120 --> 13:13.800
But that was as far as our conversation got.

218
13:13.880 --> 13:16.280
-She disappeared first. -Shit!

219
13:16.360 --> 13:19.880
Vann. You talk to everyone from people to ghosts now?

220
13:21.240 --> 13:24.080
If you guys want to know how this will turn out, have Nay read the cards.

221
13:24.160 --> 13:26.320
I'm not doing that. It's nonsense.

222
13:26.400 --> 13:28.160
Reading the cards won't change anything.

223
13:28.240 --> 13:29.760
You guys know how to read cards too?

224
13:30.480 --> 13:31.560
Interested?

225
13:32.080 --> 13:34.120
If you are, I can read the cards for you.

226
13:34.720 --> 13:35.880
I am.

227
13:36.440 --> 13:38.160
Come on. Let's do it after we eat.

228
13:39.960 --> 13:40.920
Eat up.

229
13:41.000 --> 13:42.240
Your boyfriend is superstitious.

230
13:43.240 --> 13:44.760
I told you, he's not my boyfriend.

231
13:49.240 --> 13:50.120
What do you want to do? Go ahead.

232
13:50.800 --> 13:52.520
Who is the ghost following me?

233
14:00.120 --> 14:02.040
Looks like she's been around for a very long time.

234
14:02.120 --> 14:06.040
She could be your ancestor or someone who's watching over you.

235
14:07.000 --> 14:08.400
When she appeared,

236
14:08.480 --> 14:10.560
judging by the way she was dressed,

237
14:10.640 --> 14:12.480
she must've been your Yong ancestor.

238
14:13.600 --> 14:14.680
Yong?

239
14:15.360 --> 14:17.240
-Ramyun? -No.

240
14:18.880 --> 14:20.640
So what does she want?

241
14:29.440 --> 14:30.840
She won't tell us.

242
14:32.360 --> 14:34.400
If I make merit for her, will she stop following me?

243
14:40.320 --> 14:41.720
She won't tell us.

244
14:41.800 --> 14:43.440
And she covered the cards so we couldn't see them.

245
14:48.600 --> 14:49.520
Vann.

246
14:50.960 --> 14:52.040
You've only seen her once?

247
14:52.920 --> 14:54.160
Yeah, I've only seen her once.

248
14:54.680 --> 14:56.000
But it took so much to get her to appear.

249
14:56.080 --> 14:59.120
Maybe next time, I'll actually have to kiss Rakkhun.

250
14:59.200 --> 15:00.040
-A kiss? -A kiss?

251
15:00.120 --> 15:00.960
Come on, Vann.

252
15:01.040 --> 15:02.240
Like, kiss-kiss?

253
15:02.920 --> 15:04.000
It's a long story.

254
15:04.080 --> 15:05.400
I'll tell you later.

255
15:06.400 --> 15:08.320
But I need to find a way to talk to her first.

256
15:10.320 --> 15:12.200
Does she have to be the one to come to you?

257
15:14.240 --> 15:17.280
If I don't wait for her to appear, what do you expect me to do?

258
15:18.040 --> 15:19.240
Go out and find her?

259
15:19.840 --> 15:21.080
I don't want to die yet.

260
15:23.280 --> 15:25.240
We don't have to go find her.

261
15:26.880 --> 15:28.280
Because we can summon her.

262
15:28.360 --> 15:29.720
How?

263
15:29.800 --> 15:31.440
Do you have her number?

264
15:33.600 --> 15:34.840
You want him to call the ghost?

265
15:41.800 --> 15:43.440
Is this how you summon a ghost?

266
15:44.360 --> 15:45.200
Yes.

267
15:45.280 --> 15:48.480
My family usually performs this ritual at the ancestral spirit shrine.

268
15:48.560 --> 15:49.800
Then the ghost appears.

269
15:50.680 --> 15:52.040
Didn't you say you've never seen a ghost?

270
15:52.760 --> 15:54.520
I've never seen one directly.

271
15:55.040 --> 15:56.640
But I've seen one through a spirit medium.

272
15:57.560 --> 16:00.840
Usually, one person in my family is chosen to be the spirit medium.

273
16:00.920 --> 16:03.800
And everyone in the family can talk to our ancestors through them.

274
16:10.600 --> 16:12.920
If the ghost appears here, who'll be the medium?

275
16:14.040 --> 16:16.360
If the ghost appears, you can see her.

276
16:16.440 --> 16:18.120
So we don't need a medium.

277
16:20.240 --> 16:22.320
Hey! Do we have to light incense too?

278
16:22.400 --> 16:24.840
Of course. The incense is important.

279
16:26.120 --> 16:27.480
Fine, light it.

280
16:28.000 --> 16:30.040
But be careful. Don't let anything catch fire.

281
16:30.920 --> 16:32.760
Or all my dinosaurs will go extinct.

282
16:34.120 --> 16:35.600
What should I do?

283
16:35.680 --> 16:36.640
I forgot the chant.

284
16:39.200 --> 16:40.440
Will the ghost even appear?

285
16:40.520 --> 16:42.600
I'm not usually the one who chants.

286
16:43.440 --> 16:44.760
Then who usually does it?

287
16:44.840 --> 16:46.440
Can you call and ask them?

288
16:48.120 --> 16:49.240
My grandmother.

289
16:49.960 --> 16:51.240
But I've recorded her before.

290
16:51.320 --> 16:54.040
Because my mother once made me memorize this chant.

291
16:59.120 --> 17:01.560
Sacred beings of the northern skies.

292
17:02.200 --> 17:04.599
-I'll transcribe it and try chanting it. -Please open the path between worlds.

293
17:05.839 --> 17:06.880
By the time you're done,

294
17:06.960 --> 17:08.560
we'll probably be chanting it next month.

295
17:08.640 --> 17:09.760
Then what would you do?

296
17:09.839 --> 17:11.760
Just have your grandmother chant it.

297
17:12.400 --> 17:15.040
You mean play the recording and perform the ritual at the same time?

298
17:15.119 --> 17:16.960
This is the age of technology.

299
17:17.040 --> 17:18.400
Your ancestors…

300
17:18.480 --> 17:20.079
They probably won't mind.

301
17:24.760 --> 17:27.839
Sacred beings of the northern skies,

302
17:27.920 --> 17:30.280
please open the path between worlds.

303
17:30.360 --> 17:32.920
Let the voices of the descendants reach the departed.

304
17:33.520 --> 17:35.360
Om, spirits of the household,

305
17:35.880 --> 17:38.360
spirits of the family line, elders,

306
17:38.960 --> 17:40.120
forefathers and foremothers,

307
17:41.160 --> 17:42.840
those who once built homes,

308
17:42.920 --> 17:45.320
worked the fields, planted rice,

309
17:45.400 --> 17:47.200
-Do you see a ghost? -and raised children.

310
17:47.720 --> 17:48.720
-No. -Now…

311
17:48.800 --> 17:50.920
-I don't see anything. -We will light incense.

312
17:51.000 --> 17:54.760
May you hear this voice from wherever you are.

313
17:55.360 --> 17:56.800
-I don't think it's working. -Please come down to this house

314
17:56.880 --> 17:58.560
-If she were coming, she'd be here by now. -to receive

315
17:58.640 --> 17:59.640
-Pack it up. -the offerings,

316
17:59.720 --> 18:00.840
Wait.

317
18:00.920 --> 18:04.480
-Can you wait until the incense burns out? -including food and water.

318
18:13.360 --> 18:14.280
She's here.

319
18:14.360 --> 18:15.880
Garlah is here.

320
18:16.520 --> 18:17.720
I don't think that's her.

321
18:17.800 --> 18:19.800
What kind of ghost has such good manners?

322
18:19.880 --> 18:21.480
It even knocked first.

323
18:24.920 --> 18:27.040
Linda sent me to ask if you guys are having dinner together.

324
18:27.640 --> 18:29.960
I am. An army marches on its stomach.

325
18:30.040 --> 18:31.240
Tell her to make some for me.

326
18:32.560 --> 18:33.720
You guys aren't done yet?

327
18:34.240 --> 18:35.200
Almost.

328
18:45.560 --> 18:46.920
What do you want to do?

329
18:47.000 --> 18:48.200
You want to wait until the incense burns out, right?

330
18:49.360 --> 18:51.280
I don't think this method is really going to work.

331
18:53.920 --> 18:55.360
Are you that disappointed?

332
18:57.360 --> 18:58.440
A little.

333
18:59.520 --> 19:01.440
I've dealt with things like this my whole life.

334
19:01.520 --> 19:04.000
I don't want to put up with this anymore.

335
19:08.160 --> 19:09.440
Do you trust me?

336
19:10.040 --> 19:10.960
I do.

337
19:11.840 --> 19:14.400
Otherwise, I wouldn't have pestered you into taking the job.

338
19:18.440 --> 19:19.440
Then let me apologize in advance.

339
20:07.400 --> 20:08.760
Nothing's happening.

340
20:15.560 --> 20:16.760
Wait, Vann.

341
20:26.800 --> 20:27.880
She's here.

342
20:27.960 --> 20:29.160
It actually worked.

343
20:29.240 --> 20:30.960
-Hey, you! -Stay right there.

344
20:33.600 --> 20:36.680
Hey, you. I thought you weren't coming.

345
20:37.280 --> 20:38.840
You're pretty naughty, aren't you?

346
20:38.920 --> 20:40.280
Incense doesn't work on you,

347
20:40.360 --> 20:42.360
but the moment we kissed, you showed up.

348
20:42.440 --> 20:46.160
But thank you for not losing your temper and throwing a knife at us like last time.

349
20:46.240 --> 20:48.960
Vann, how can you provoke her like that?

350
20:49.040 --> 20:50.320
You'll get hurt again.

351
20:50.920 --> 20:52.320
Trust me.

352
20:52.400 --> 20:54.320
Just watch a pro at work.

353
20:56.840 --> 20:58.000
I'll get straight to the point.

354
20:58.520 --> 21:00.880
My eyes get tired just looking at you and your bug eyes.

355
21:01.560 --> 21:02.560
My Rakkhun here

356
21:02.640 --> 21:06.240
wants to know why you keep stopping him from finding love.

357
21:06.320 --> 21:07.880
And with my male friends too.

358
21:07.960 --> 21:10.360
Yeah. His male friends too.

359
21:11.000 --> 21:13.240
Why do you keep haunting the men who get close to him

360
21:13.320 --> 21:15.120
until he has no one left?

361
21:15.200 --> 21:16.520
No friends.

362
21:16.600 --> 21:17.800
And his boyfriends left him.

363
21:17.880 --> 21:19.600
You don't have to rub it in.

364
21:21.280 --> 21:22.240
Stay quiet.

365
21:23.560 --> 21:25.200
I'll kill you!

366
21:25.800 --> 21:26.840
Okay.

367
21:27.360 --> 21:28.640
If you want to kill me, go ahead.

368
21:28.720 --> 21:30.280
But let me hear your reason first.

369
21:30.360 --> 21:32.160
Why do you keep tormenting Rakkhun?

370
21:32.240 --> 21:34.200
Aren't you his ancestor?

371
21:34.840 --> 21:36.080
I'm not tormenting him.

372
21:36.680 --> 21:39.000
I'm protecting him from bad people.

373
21:41.400 --> 21:44.320
Someday, he'll understand.

374
21:44.840 --> 21:46.240
Understand what?

375
21:46.320 --> 21:47.360
Are you delusional?

376
21:47.440 --> 21:50.280
You're traumatizing him.

377
21:50.960 --> 21:54.080
He's afraid to live his life or even let himself be happy.

378
21:55.280 --> 21:57.280
Now I understand why you haven't been reincarnated.

379
21:57.360 --> 22:00.600
It's because you're this kind of ghost that you're stuck here like--

380
22:03.560 --> 22:04.400
Vann!

381
22:11.080 --> 22:13.360
Garlah! Don't hurt him!

382
22:14.240 --> 22:15.880
Garlah! Stop it right now!

383
22:17.320 --> 22:19.320
Garlah! Please stop!

384
22:20.400 --> 22:23.080
Garlah! Stop it! Enough!

385
22:23.160 --> 22:24.640
I'm begging you.

386
22:27.160 --> 22:28.400
Please stop.

387
22:37.040 --> 22:39.080
Vann! Are you hurt?

388
22:39.160 --> 22:40.520
Are you okay?

389
23:08.880 --> 23:10.640
Don't worry about it.

390
23:10.720 --> 23:12.080
I'm fine.

391
23:12.960 --> 23:14.680
This is nothing. She can't hurt me.

392
23:17.440 --> 23:19.400
Tonight, I'm going back to sleep at my condo.

393
23:20.200 --> 23:21.600
And I'm going to cancel the job.

394
23:22.160 --> 23:24.000
I'll talk to Linda myself.

395
23:26.880 --> 23:28.280
Why are you canceling?

396
23:28.360 --> 23:29.600
Rakkhun.

397
23:30.480 --> 23:32.120
Garlah finally talked to me.

398
23:32.200 --> 23:33.560
Just give me some time.

399
23:34.160 --> 23:35.560
Every time Garlah appears,

400
23:35.640 --> 23:37.400
you always get hurt.

401
23:37.480 --> 23:41.040
Do you have to get your neck broken before this job can end?

402
23:41.640 --> 23:43.680
I can't be responsible for your life.

403
23:44.280 --> 23:46.560
You don't have to be responsible for me.

404
23:46.640 --> 23:48.160
I chose to take this job.

405
23:48.240 --> 23:50.000
When the job's done, I get paid.

406
23:50.080 --> 23:51.600
See? It's a win-win for both of us.

407
23:53.320 --> 23:54.720
Do you want the money that badly?

408
23:56.960 --> 23:59.720
You want money so badly that you don't even care about your own life?

409
24:02.800 --> 24:03.720
Yeah.

410
24:04.560 --> 24:05.680
I want the money.

411
24:06.400 --> 24:07.840
Or I wouldn't have taken this job.

412
24:11.920 --> 24:13.840
I'll pay you the full fee.

413
24:15.480 --> 24:17.080
And we don't have to see each other again.

414
24:17.840 --> 24:19.360
I'm ending the job here.

415
24:26.760 --> 24:28.080
Rakkhun, wait.

416
24:28.160 --> 24:30.080
This isn't how you solve the problem.

417
24:30.680 --> 24:33.560
You know Garlah will show up again if you have a boyfriend.

418
24:34.160 --> 24:35.560
Forget it.

419
24:36.240 --> 24:38.960
If it's that difficult, then I just won't have one.

420
24:40.640 --> 24:42.680
I won't die just because I don't have love in my life.

421
25:05.000 --> 25:08.200
Let me whisper softly

422
25:24.760 --> 25:26.040
Where are you?

423
25:26.120 --> 25:27.520
Everyone’s waiting in the music rehearsal room.

424
25:30.080 --> 25:31.640
You guys go ahead and practice.

425
25:31.720 --> 25:32.840
I’ll catch up with you later.

426
25:32.920 --> 25:35.920
TONHON

427
25:55.440 --> 25:57.040
I'm not trying to pressure you.

428
25:57.640 --> 26:00.560
It's just that the email said the result was still pending.

429
26:00.640 --> 26:03.920
So I came to ask if you've made a decision yet.

430
26:05.080 --> 26:06.200
I haven't thought about it yet.

431
26:06.720 --> 26:08.360
I have a lot of other things to do.

432
26:08.960 --> 26:10.200
Excuse me.

433
26:10.280 --> 26:11.680
Wait.

434
26:13.120 --> 26:14.160
You should back off

435
26:14.760 --> 26:16.800
before I reject your offer.

436
26:32.840 --> 26:36.640
I heard you want to apply to be a singer here.

437
26:37.240 --> 26:38.160
Yes.

438
26:38.240 --> 26:40.120
You can audition me first.

439
26:40.200 --> 26:42.280
I can play guitar. I can dance.

440
26:42.360 --> 26:44.400
I can definitely entertain the customers here.

441
26:44.480 --> 26:46.320
I guarantee they won't get bored.

442
26:50.000 --> 26:53.200
I suppose this is one way for you to convince Phatee

443
26:53.280 --> 26:54.920
to take your job, right?

444
26:58.440 --> 27:01.680
To be honest, customers…

445
27:02.840 --> 27:04.240
I want them too.

446
27:05.000 --> 27:08.000
But I'm really not sure if the money I'd spend on you

447
27:08.720 --> 27:11.440
would be worth what I'd get in return.

448
27:13.600 --> 27:15.000
Then…

449
27:16.720 --> 27:18.240
what if you didn't have to pay me?

450
27:19.600 --> 27:21.240
I'm willing to sing here for free.

451
27:22.120 --> 27:24.280
As long as I get to sing with Phatee.

452
27:28.640 --> 27:30.760
-For free? -Yes.

453
27:33.800 --> 27:35.160
Deal.

454
27:51.760 --> 27:53.200
We're closed.

455
27:57.520 --> 28:02.320
Sitting here from opening until closing like this isn't going to work.

456
28:02.400 --> 28:03.920
I'm not taking your job no matter what.

457
28:04.520 --> 28:06.800
Today, I'm here as a customer of the bar.

458
28:07.320 --> 28:09.760
Or if you change your mind, you can tell me.

459
28:10.520 --> 28:11.560
No way.

460
28:39.720 --> 28:41.040
Kind.

461
28:41.120 --> 28:42.280
Warm.

462
28:42.880 --> 28:44.200
Caring.

463
28:44.280 --> 28:45.800
Idealistic.

464
28:47.040 --> 28:48.760
You have all the traits of a male lead.

465
28:50.920 --> 28:52.760
You're drunk, but you're still writing fiction.

466
28:53.280 --> 28:55.440
Are all writers as delusional as you?

467
28:57.400 --> 28:58.480
I'll take you home.

468
28:59.280 --> 29:00.480
Stay still for a second.

469
29:09.760 --> 29:10.760
Can you walk?

470
29:17.440 --> 29:18.880
Watch where you're going.

471
29:36.280 --> 29:37.200
Hey.

472
29:38.160 --> 29:39.920
What's wrong? Why are you drinking alone?

473
29:42.440 --> 29:43.760
I'm feeling a little down.

474
29:44.360 --> 29:45.880
I'll turn off the lights.

475
29:56.200 --> 29:58.000
You don't usually drink.

476
29:59.160 --> 30:01.280
Why? Did something bad happen?

477
30:03.800 --> 30:05.400
It's not that bad.

478
30:07.040 --> 30:08.200
Since we're already at it,

479
30:08.280 --> 30:10.120
I might as well ask you.

480
30:10.200 --> 30:11.480
Go ahead.

481
30:13.720 --> 30:15.480
Today, I summoned the ghost.

482
30:16.000 --> 30:17.480
And I talked to her for a bit.

483
30:19.000 --> 30:20.440
Then the ghost strangled me.

484
30:21.040 --> 30:21.960
Right here.

485
30:25.400 --> 30:26.360
She strangled you pretty hard.

486
30:26.960 --> 30:27.920
So?

487
30:28.520 --> 30:31.360
You don't want this job because the ghost strangled you?

488
30:32.080 --> 30:33.400
No.

489
30:33.480 --> 30:35.040
I want to keep going.

490
30:35.840 --> 30:37.600
But Rakkhun wants to cancel.

491
30:38.280 --> 30:39.840
I seriously don't get it.

492
30:41.000 --> 30:43.040
I followed the entire brief

493
30:43.120 --> 30:44.720
so I could finish the job as fast as possible.

494
30:46.240 --> 30:48.600
But suddenly today, Rakkhun got mad at me.

495
30:49.480 --> 30:50.800
I called, but he didn't answer.

496
30:51.400 --> 30:52.800
I texted, but he didn't reply.

497
30:54.160 --> 30:55.640
I don't know if he can be alone.

498
30:55.720 --> 30:57.360
He's already such a scaredy-cat.

499
30:58.560 --> 31:00.400
And he's been studying hard lately.

500
31:01.360 --> 31:03.000
He hasn't been sleeping well.

501
31:03.600 --> 31:05.360
If he gets sick, who's going to take care of him?

502
31:08.200 --> 31:10.600
Rakkhun is probably worried about you.

503
31:10.680 --> 31:12.400
Just like you're worried about Rakkhun.

504
31:13.000 --> 31:14.000
I'm not worried about him.

505
31:14.080 --> 31:15.680
I'm more worried about my money.

506
31:19.880 --> 31:21.280
You're afraid he won't be able to sleep.

507
31:21.360 --> 31:22.760
You're afraid he'll see the ghost?

508
31:22.840 --> 31:23.840
You're worried about the money?

509
31:25.440 --> 31:26.520
You're worried about him.

510
31:26.600 --> 31:27.840
You just won't admit it.

511
31:36.720 --> 31:39.960
Ask yourself how you really feel, then go talk to him.

512
31:40.040 --> 31:42.800
There's no point sitting here sad and drinking beer.

513
31:42.880 --> 31:44.120
It's just a waste of beer.

514
31:49.960 --> 31:50.920
I'll take it, then.

515
32:42.040 --> 32:44.680
VANN

516
32:55.160 --> 32:56.080
VANN: CAN I TALK TO YOU FOR A MOMENT?

517
32:56.160 --> 32:57.480
Can I talk to you for a moment?

518
32:58.680 --> 33:00.240
-Hello. -Which one's yours?

519
33:00.320 --> 33:01.600
-This one. -Okay.

520
33:03.920 --> 33:05.160
-This one's yours, right? -Yeah.

521
33:05.240 --> 33:06.800
It's a semi-detached house.

522
33:07.560 --> 33:09.320
It's nice. Not bad.

523
33:09.400 --> 33:10.360
Thanks.

524
33:13.040 --> 33:15.840
-Yay! -Yay!

525
33:15.920 --> 33:17.600
Our group is so good. We all got A's.

526
33:17.680 --> 33:18.680
Yeah.

527
33:18.760 --> 33:19.640
What do you guys say?

528
33:19.720 --> 33:21.120
Should we celebrate tonight?

529
33:21.640 --> 33:22.880
You're acting like we've graduated.

530
33:23.400 --> 33:25.040
Come on.

531
33:25.120 --> 33:28.400
People who want to drink can always find a reason to drink.

532
33:28.480 --> 33:30.520
So, what do you guys say? Who's going?

533
33:30.600 --> 33:32.000
-So I can book a table. -I'm in.

534
33:32.080 --> 33:33.280
-Me too. -You guys in the back, you coming?

535
33:33.360 --> 33:34.800
-I'm in. -Me too.

536
33:35.440 --> 33:36.440
Let's drink!

537
33:37.160 --> 33:38.720
Okay, I'm in.

538
33:38.800 --> 33:39.800
Okay.

539
33:39.880 --> 33:42.480
And Rakkhun, are you coming?

540
33:51.600 --> 33:52.600
Come with us.

541
33:53.120 --> 33:55.520
I want you to come too.

542
33:55.600 --> 33:56.960
We haven't had drinks together in ages.

543
33:58.920 --> 34:01.040
It's fun when a bunch of us go together.

544
34:03.960 --> 34:05.160
Okay, I'll come too.

545
34:05.760 --> 34:07.760
Fabulous!

546
34:07.840 --> 34:10.120
We're going drinking tonight!

547
34:10.199 --> 34:12.239
-Book us a table. -Let's celebrate!

548
34:16.320 --> 34:17.560
These are noodles from my shop.

549
34:17.639 --> 34:19.440
I don't know if there's enough for everyone.

550
34:19.960 --> 34:21.480
This is a lot. There's definitely enough for everyone.

551
34:21.560 --> 34:23.080
Thank you so much.

552
34:24.440 --> 34:26.199
Vann's here just in time.

553
34:26.280 --> 34:29.360
Then, I'll get going.

554
34:29.440 --> 34:31.040
-I'll go check on the shop. -Sure.

555
34:31.120 --> 34:32.040
Make yourself at home.

556
34:32.120 --> 34:33.280
Thank you so much.

557
34:38.719 --> 34:40.679
What's with that hair color?

558
34:41.280 --> 34:42.520
We haven't seen each other in a year.

559
34:42.600 --> 34:44.280
Shouldn't you ask how I've been?

560
34:44.360 --> 34:46.239
And you're asking about my hair color?

561
34:46.840 --> 34:48.600
I brought you some noodles.

562
34:48.679 --> 34:50.320
I saw there were a lot of people here,

563
34:50.400 --> 34:51.880
so I brought a bunch of bags.

564
34:52.880 --> 34:54.040
Thanks.

565
34:55.880 --> 34:56.800
That's it?

566
34:58.440 --> 34:59.640
Hey.

567
34:59.720 --> 35:01.280
I'm seriously asking you.

568
35:01.360 --> 35:03.120
What's better about this place than our home?

569
35:03.200 --> 35:04.760
Why won't you come home?

570
35:05.440 --> 35:06.600
You want me to come back?

571
35:06.680 --> 35:08.120
But you're the one who kicked me out.

572
35:08.200 --> 35:11.600
How was I supposed to know you'd actually leave?

573
35:12.200 --> 35:13.800
I said it in the heat of the moment.

574
35:13.880 --> 35:15.400
Couldn't you tell?

575
35:16.040 --> 35:17.240
Why didn't you tell me you were coming?

576
35:17.840 --> 35:20.840
I'm going to a funeral nearby, so I stopped by to see you.

577
35:21.640 --> 35:22.480
Whose funeral?

578
35:22.560 --> 35:24.240
Aunt Nid's.

579
35:24.320 --> 35:25.440
She had cancer.

580
35:25.520 --> 35:27.680
She died not long after she was diagnosed.

581
35:28.280 --> 35:29.720
Aunt Nid is a relative on Dad's side.

582
35:29.800 --> 35:31.080
Then why didn't Dad come too?

583
35:31.160 --> 35:34.360
Your dad didn't get along with Aunt Nid.

584
35:34.440 --> 35:36.920
I didn't want other people gossiping about us,

585
35:37.000 --> 35:39.200
so I just went to get it over with.

586
35:39.280 --> 35:41.640
Let people say whatever they want, Mom.

587
35:41.720 --> 35:43.200
Even Buddha was gossiped about.

588
35:43.280 --> 35:45.960
Wow, you dare lecture me, Vann?

589
35:46.040 --> 35:48.160
Okay, enough about this.

590
35:49.680 --> 35:52.440
Right, I've saved enough to study abroad now.

591
35:52.960 --> 35:54.600
If I finish this job, I can go right away.

592
35:55.240 --> 35:57.240
You really want to go study, right?

593
35:57.320 --> 35:59.200
You're not going just to spite me, right?

594
35:59.800 --> 36:01.080
I really want to go.

595
36:01.160 --> 36:02.640
It's my dream.

596
36:05.760 --> 36:08.120
Then I'd better get to the funeral.

597
36:08.200 --> 36:09.320
I'm leaving.

598
36:11.080 --> 36:12.200
I'll see you off.

599
36:12.840 --> 36:15.480
No need. I can go by myself.

600
36:15.560 --> 36:17.520
Focus on your work.

601
36:27.640 --> 36:28.480
Vann.

602
36:30.440 --> 36:31.760
How's your job going?

603
36:34.600 --> 36:36.360
I heard you had a fight with the client.

604
36:36.440 --> 36:38.520
Did Rakkhun come to cancel the job with you?

605
36:39.120 --> 36:40.280
He came to talk to me.

606
36:40.800 --> 36:43.120
But he hasn't officially canceled yet.

607
36:44.640 --> 36:46.280
Go sort things out with him properly.

608
36:47.040 --> 36:48.680
Don't let it become a problem.

609
37:02.120 --> 37:03.560
Here's your drink.

610
37:03.640 --> 37:05.080
Thirsty, huh?

611
37:05.160 --> 37:07.560
-You chugged that down fast. -Two glasses now.

612
37:07.640 --> 37:08.840
The beer's here.

613
37:10.520 --> 37:13.160
Why hasn't Linda dropped this supplier already?

614
37:14.960 --> 37:16.120
Other people need it too.

615
37:17.000 --> 37:18.280
Hey.

616
37:19.120 --> 37:20.680
Why are you complaining?

617
37:20.760 --> 37:23.200
You'll have to work together someday anyway, right?

618
37:23.280 --> 37:25.560
You two should get along.

619
37:25.640 --> 37:27.080
There's no need, Mimi.

620
37:28.760 --> 37:30.720
Actually, we already know each other very well.

621
37:31.560 --> 37:33.200
Because I know him so well,

622
37:33.280 --> 37:34.680
I don't want to know him anymore.

623
37:34.760 --> 37:36.320
Know each other well?

624
37:39.120 --> 37:40.520
Here's the beer bill.

625
37:43.000 --> 37:45.360
I'll take care of this bill.

626
37:45.880 --> 37:46.920
By the way,

627
37:47.440 --> 37:51.200
you two have known each other for a long time, right?

628
37:52.000 --> 37:53.160
You know him that well?

629
37:53.240 --> 37:55.400
And you know him so well you don't want to know him…

630
37:55.480 --> 37:57.240
You two are exes, aren't you?

631
37:57.320 --> 37:58.240
Mimi!

632
38:00.280 --> 38:01.520
You could say that.

633
38:03.960 --> 38:06.000
Actually, it started with us being friends.

634
38:16.560 --> 38:18.000
Thank you so much for today.

635
38:18.880 --> 38:19.800
I'm chill.

636
38:20.720 --> 38:23.280
I'm glad you agreed to go drinking.

637
38:25.440 --> 38:27.440
Going once in a while is fun too.

638
38:29.880 --> 38:30.760
Rakkhun.

639
38:31.480 --> 38:33.200
Can I ask you something?

640
38:34.640 --> 38:37.280
I don't know if I can ask you this.

641
38:38.080 --> 38:39.240
But I want to know,

642
38:40.400 --> 38:42.760
the guy who picked you up at the faculty building that day,

643
38:43.280 --> 38:44.120
who is he?

644
38:47.680 --> 38:48.800
He's an older guy I know.

645
38:51.640 --> 38:52.680
An older guy?

646
38:54.760 --> 38:56.520
I know everyone in your life.

647
38:57.120 --> 38:59.640
You're not someone who lets just anyone into your life.

648
39:04.000 --> 39:05.440
I'll be straight with you.

649
39:07.280 --> 39:08.800
You've moved on from me, right?

650
39:09.440 --> 39:10.760
So I can come to terms with it.

651
39:12.080 --> 39:13.440
It's not like that.

652
39:14.560 --> 39:15.440
It's complicated.

653
39:16.040 --> 39:18.000
We're not seeing each other or anything.

654
39:19.480 --> 39:22.280
That means I still have a chance, right?

655
39:28.360 --> 39:29.920
I think you should move on.

656
39:32.200 --> 39:34.400
Let's each go live our own lives.

657
39:39.680 --> 39:41.040
If you're saying this because

658
39:41.120 --> 39:42.760
you don't feel anything for me anymore,

659
39:43.720 --> 39:44.800
I'll leave you alone.

660
39:46.160 --> 39:48.560
But if you're just afraid the ghost will haunt me again,

661
39:49.240 --> 39:50.760
I'm not going anywhere.

662
39:51.440 --> 39:54.240
I won't let the ghost ruin our relationship again.

663
40:07.720 --> 40:10.280
I told you to get out of Rakkhun's life!

664
40:15.680 --> 40:16.720
Kan, what's wrong?

665
40:19.320 --> 40:20.240
I'm fine.

666
40:21.280 --> 40:22.360
I'm not afraid of ghosts.

667
40:23.720 --> 40:25.560
I'm more afraid of not being with you.

668
40:36.800 --> 40:38.000
Kan!

669
40:43.400 --> 40:44.840
Stop! Garlah!

670
40:44.920 --> 40:46.320
I told you to stop!

671
40:46.400 --> 40:47.960
Stop hurting people.

672
40:51.880 --> 40:54.000
Garlah! Stop hurting people.

673
40:54.760 --> 40:56.040
I warned you.

674
40:56.120 --> 40:57.200
You didn't listen to me!

675
40:57.840 --> 40:59.720
You'll fucking destroy yourself over a man!

676
41:00.360 --> 41:02.040
-Sicko! -Rakkhun!

677
41:20.880 --> 41:24.080
I think you should go home.

678
41:30.840 --> 41:31.880
Are you okay?

679
41:34.400 --> 41:35.480
I'm okay.

680
41:37.920 --> 41:39.600
Go shower and get some sleep.

681
41:43.600 --> 41:45.000
I'll head home now

682
41:45.080 --> 41:46.040
so you can get some rest.

683
41:47.240 --> 41:48.600
Wait.

684
41:54.400 --> 41:55.920
Can you stay with me tonight?

685
42:00.680 --> 42:03.320
Hey, can I ask you something?

686
42:04.160 --> 42:05.760
What are you going to do with the money?

687
42:05.840 --> 42:07.720
I want to study in Japan.

688
42:08.640 --> 42:11.600
Believe it or not, I graduated with a gold medal.

689
42:11.680 --> 42:13.520
And when I was an undergrad,

690
42:14.120 --> 42:15.880
I got a full scholarship too.

691
42:15.960 --> 42:19.160
Big companies were fighting over me before I even graduated.

692
42:20.440 --> 42:21.720
Then why don't you apply for a scholarship?

693
42:21.800 --> 42:23.240
With a profile this good,

694
42:23.840 --> 42:24.760
it shouldn't be that hard, right?

695
42:26.160 --> 42:27.160
I already took the exam.

696
42:27.720 --> 42:29.040
It was a full scholarship too.

697
42:29.880 --> 42:31.400
Only one person in the whole country gets it.

698
42:32.000 --> 42:33.760
I was so damn confident during the exam.

699
42:34.280 --> 42:35.360
I thought I'd definitely get it.

700
42:35.440 --> 42:38.480
You know, my whole life,

701
42:38.560 --> 42:40.080
I'd never failed an exam before.

702
42:40.160 --> 42:41.800
Until this scholarship exam.

703
42:44.200 --> 42:45.280
And I found out later that

704
42:45.360 --> 42:48.720
the person who got the scholarship fucking got it through connections.

705
42:49.320 --> 42:51.120
So I decided to earn the money myself.

706
42:51.640 --> 42:53.000
I'm not counting on those scholarships anymore.

707
42:53.960 --> 42:55.040
You're amazing.

708
42:55.120 --> 42:56.160
If it were me,

709
42:56.240 --> 42:57.560
I'd have given up already.

710
42:58.240 --> 43:01.040
Hey, Vann, I think I heard Garlah just now too.

711
43:01.840 --> 43:03.520
What did Garlah say to you?

712
43:05.440 --> 43:09.280
Garlah said my life would be ruined because of a man.

713
43:10.480 --> 43:11.480
Obviously.

714
43:12.160 --> 43:14.400
Garlah doesn't like you dating men.

715
43:14.920 --> 43:16.880
She's so fucking conservative.

716
43:17.640 --> 43:18.920
That's possible.

717
43:20.800 --> 43:22.520
Go to sleep. It's late.

718
43:41.120 --> 43:42.320
Can I hold your hand?

719
43:43.360 --> 43:44.520
It'll put me at ease.

720
44:04.480 --> 44:05.680
You can sleep here.

721
44:06.200 --> 44:07.120
I don't mind.

722
45:08.120 --> 45:09.320
Talay.

723
45:22.080 --> 45:24.320
Have you seen Talay? Isn't he here?

724
45:26.240 --> 45:27.880
He went out.

725
45:27.960 --> 45:28.880
What is it?

726
45:33.880 --> 45:34.920
Well,

727
45:36.120 --> 45:37.640
I don't know who to talk to.

728
45:38.880 --> 45:40.200
Talay isn't here either.

729
45:40.720 --> 45:42.200
This might sound a little weird,

730
45:42.280 --> 45:46.680
but have you ever liked someone or ever loved someone?

731
45:50.840 --> 45:52.600
-I have. -Who?

732
45:54.280 --> 45:55.680
I mean,

733
45:56.440 --> 45:57.760
what does it feel like?

734
45:59.560 --> 46:00.560
Who do you like, then?

735
46:01.360 --> 46:03.920
-Rakkhun? -Are you crazy?

736
46:04.840 --> 46:06.200
Just someone.

737
46:07.160 --> 46:09.240
I'm still not sure, so I came to ask.

738
46:12.280 --> 46:16.000
I was interested, curious, and restless.

739
46:16.800 --> 46:18.160
I couldn't stop thinking about him.

740
46:18.680 --> 46:19.720
That's how I knew I liked him.

741
46:23.960 --> 46:26.960
Do you feel anything strange when you're around him?

742
46:27.720 --> 46:28.720
Like,

743
46:29.720 --> 46:31.280
sleeping well,

744
46:31.800 --> 46:33.800
sometimes getting butterflies in your stomach,

745
46:33.880 --> 46:36.000
or feeling a flutter in your chest.

746
46:37.160 --> 46:39.080
Your arms and legs never seem to know where to go.

747
46:39.920 --> 46:41.240
It depends on the person.

748
46:42.240 --> 46:43.960
How do you feel when you're around him?

749
46:52.240 --> 46:54.000
Before I sleep, I think about him.

750
46:54.720 --> 46:56.200
When I wake up, I think about him.

751
46:57.280 --> 46:59.240
I expect every notification to be his message.

752
47:00.720 --> 47:02.520
I like seeing him smile.

753
47:03.840 --> 47:07.200
I want to smack myself for saying things that hurt him.

754
47:08.520 --> 47:10.520
When he can't sleep, I can't sleep either.

755
47:12.280 --> 47:14.200
When he's sad, I'm sad too.

756
47:15.760 --> 47:17.400
If his eyes well up,

757
47:17.960 --> 47:19.400
I feel like I'm going crazy.

758
47:20.360 --> 47:22.880
I'm angry at myself for not being able to do anything.

759
47:23.920 --> 47:26.040
I want to be close to him, but I can't be too close.

760
47:28.200 --> 47:29.760
Is this normal?

761
47:31.240 --> 47:32.960
Do you feel that way about me?

762
47:33.560 --> 47:34.760
About you?

763
47:35.280 --> 47:36.560
No way.

764
47:37.160 --> 47:38.680
That means that person is special to you.

765
47:40.160 --> 47:43.400
This is what having a crush on someone feels like.

766
48:01.960 --> 48:02.880
Rakkhun.

767
48:06.800 --> 48:07.920
I bought this for you.

768
48:08.560 --> 48:09.720
Thanks.

769
48:12.280 --> 48:14.640
I think you should stay away from me for now.

770
48:15.840 --> 48:17.280
You'll get hurt again.

771
48:17.360 --> 48:18.640
No.

772
48:19.160 --> 48:20.640
I want to be close to you.

773
48:21.400 --> 48:23.080
I'm not afraid of that ghost anymore.

774
48:24.040 --> 48:25.240
Look.

775
48:28.640 --> 48:30.400
I've got something powerful too.

776
48:30.480 --> 48:31.880
Whatever ghost it is, bring it on.

777
48:31.960 --> 48:32.800
I'm not afraid.

778
48:33.560 --> 48:34.720
I told you.

779
48:35.240 --> 48:36.840
I'm not leaving you again.

780
48:54.680 --> 48:56.000
Whoa.

781
48:56.080 --> 48:57.800
You look so handsome today.

782
48:57.880 --> 48:58.840
Like a model.

783
48:58.920 --> 49:00.360
Where are you going to model?

784
49:00.440 --> 49:02.240
I'm here to take you back to the condo.

785
49:02.960 --> 49:04.480
And then I'll take you out to eat.

786
49:04.560 --> 49:06.400
I happened to get a voucher.

787
49:07.000 --> 49:08.000
It's a Michelin restaurant.

788
49:09.520 --> 49:11.440
I have a study session with friends.

789
49:12.600 --> 49:15.160
By the way, I can still save this voucher for later, right?

790
49:16.840 --> 49:18.000
Sure.

791
49:18.760 --> 49:20.080
Want me to pick you up?

792
49:20.600 --> 49:21.440
Where are you studying?

793
49:25.480 --> 49:26.720
At my house.

794
49:27.480 --> 49:29.240
I'll pick him up and drop him off myself.

795
49:29.840 --> 49:31.240
I'll take good care of him.

796
49:34.080 --> 49:35.160
You don't have to worry.

797
49:35.240 --> 49:36.200
I'll let you know when I get there.

798
49:38.880 --> 49:39.760
Take good care of yourself.

799
49:39.840 --> 49:42.440
Okay. I'm going.

800
50:06.600 --> 50:07.880
Garlah, where are you?

801
50:07.960 --> 50:09.240
Come out and talk to me.

802
50:10.440 --> 50:11.480
You don't have to hide.

803
50:11.560 --> 50:13.840
You can come into my dreams almost every night,

804
50:13.920 --> 50:15.440
so just coming out to talk

805
50:15.520 --> 50:16.920
can't be that hard, can it?

806
50:36.560 --> 50:38.720
Okay. Now we can talk.

807
50:40.720 --> 50:42.240
Let's make a deal.

808
51:41.880 --> 51:46.560
If Rakkhun gets hurt dating a man, you're dead!

809
51:46.640 --> 51:49.080
Taking your job doesn't mean I'll help you.

810
51:49.160 --> 51:50.600
Are you just fucking with me,

811
51:50.680 --> 51:52.080
or are you just making excuses to be with me?

812
51:53.080 --> 51:54.320
The male lead in my novel is the same.

813
51:54.400 --> 51:56.040
I already picture him as you.

814
51:56.120 --> 51:57.680
So it has to be you.

815
51:57.760 --> 51:59.160
Customers aren't allowed back here.

816
51:59.240 --> 52:00.720
I'm not here as a customer.

817
52:00.800 --> 52:02.440
Today, I'm here as a singer.

818
52:02.520 --> 52:04.080
What I want is to finish the job.

819
52:04.160 --> 52:06.040
So I can go study like I planned.

820
52:06.120 --> 52:07.960
Kissing me, sleeping with me,

821
52:08.040 --> 52:09.040
always texting me,

822
52:09.120 --> 52:10.720
was all of that just for the job?
